-- OAUH2 FLOW
1. Client (web app) request a creatdential from Authorise server (google, github)
2. oauth server provide a client id and client secret for client
3. User was also trusted by oauth server (google or gihub)
4. when user login to Client (web app) they was redirect to oauth server to verify and get token
5. user sent included the token into request sent to resource server to get the response

-- incrypt decrypt with sops
1, install age age-keygent https://github.com/FiloSottile/age/releases
2. move file to C:\Program Files\age\
3. Add that folder to Environment Variables → PATH
4. age-keygen --version
5. install sops
6. generate key
mkdir %USERPROFILE%\.config\sops\age
age-keygen -o %USERPROFILE%\.config\sops\age\keys.txt
7. Copy the public key
8. create .sops.yaml file
creation_rules:
  - encrypted_regex: 'client-secret'
    age: age1k9xv8z...
9. encrypt the file
sops -e -i application.yaml
10. rename the encrypted file
mv application.yaml application.enc.yaml

-- before run in local
11 get private key: type %USERPROFILE%\.config\sops\age\keys.txt
12. tell sops which key:
setx SOPS_AGE_KEY_FILE "%USERPROFILE%\.config\sops\age\keys.txt"
close and open terminal again
13. decrypt file
sops -d application.enc.yaml > application.yaml



-- example age keygen
age-keygen: warning: writing secret key to a world-readable file
Public key: age1svk0zlz35ljh552ujztsy6xncd48ckwyezed5zgxswsn2rs7sdeqyz64nr